Fixed. `enqueue` now checks `queue.remaining` before touching the store, then writes all enqueue records and calls the atomic `enqueueMany`. A refused batch throws `QueueFullError` with zero side effects; an accepted one still writes one record per job and queues all of them.

Added to `test/integration.test.js`:
- refused batch: store file byte-identical and queue contents unchanged
- accepted batch: one enqueue record per job and all jobs queued in order

`node --test`: 67 passing.
